  "text": {
    "intro": "The preserves tent is the most competitive building at the show, and the only one with a locked door.\nFive entrants are involved. Determine each entrant's price, preserve and ingredient.\n- **Entrant**: Ottilie, Emeka, Harriet, Bernadette and Stanislaw.\n- **Price** (listed from cheaper to dearer): $3, $5, $7, $9 and $11.\n- **Preserve**: rosehip syrup; hot pepper jelly; green walnut pickle; quince jelly; and sloe and apple butter.\n- **Secret ingredient**: star anise, orange zest, a splash of gin, black pepper and nothing whatsoever.\nEvery entrant has a different price, preserve and ingredient, so within each category every item is used exactly once.",
    "clues": [
      "The entrant who adds nothing whatsoever and $5 are exactly one price step apart in price order, in one direction or the other. Bernadette charges $5.",
      "The entrant who adds star anise charges $3.",
      "Stanislaw is exactly one price step cheaper than $9, with no price in between. The entrant who adds black pepper does not charge $9.",
      "The entrant who adds a splash of gin is dearer than $5 in price order.",
      "The entrant who enters green walnut pickle is cheaper than $11 in price order.",
      "Emeka is exactly one price step cheaper than the entrant who enters green walnut pickle, with no price in between.",
      "Ottilie is cheaper than the entrant who enters hot pepper jelly in price order.",
      "The entrant who enters rosehip syrup and the entrant who adds a splash of gin are exactly one price step apart in price order, in one direction or the other.",
      "Bernadette is exactly one price step cheaper than the entrant who enters quince jelly, with no price in between."
